-- title:
--   Level-raising rung at p with η-factor α²-1
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring which is a domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal and with finite residue field; $p$ is a prime with $p\neq 2$ and $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$.
--
--   **Residual data.** $\bar\rho$ is a [`ResidualGaloisRep`](def/GaloisRep_Residual.html#L22) over $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$: a $k$-vector space $\bar\rho.V$ of rank $2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ (realised as $\mathbb Q$-algebra automorphisms of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb Q$) to $\mathrm{End}_k(\bar\rho.V)$ which is trivial on the automorphisms fixing some finite subextension. The hypothesis `habs` says that the base change of $\bar\rho$ to $\overline k$ has no invariant subspace other than $\bot$ and $\top$; `hord` says that the $\mathcal O$-adic representation [`GaloisRepAdic.ofResidualGaloisRep ρbar`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L196) is ordinary at $p$, i.e. for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ in its non-units there is a line $L=k\cdot b_0$ spanned by the first vector of a basis, stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$, on which inertia acts trivially modulo $L$.
--
--   **The set $S$ and the level $N$.** $S$ is a finite set of primes containing $p$ (`hS`, `hpS`); $N$ is a non-zero level with $N p\neq 0$, $p\nmid N$ and every prime divisor of $N$ in $S$ (`hpN`, `hNS`).
--
--   **Shape of the level (the group `Smin`).** $Smin\subseteq S$ contains $p$, and for primes $q\neq p$ one has $q\in Smin$ iff $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$ (`hmin`); every $q\in Smin$ with $q\neq p$ divides $N$ (`hNmin`); a prime $q\neq p$ not in $Smin$ which divides $N$ divides it with exponent at least $2$ (`hNunr`); no prime $q\neq p$ has $q^3\mid N$ (`hN3`); and at each $q\in Smin$, $q\neq p$, the adic representation attached to $\bar\rho$ has $\mathrm{charpoly}=(X-1)^2$ on inertia (`htame`).
--
--   **Ihara hypothesis at $p$ (`hihara`).** For every $\mathcal O$-module $A$, every non-zero $\ell_0$ and every $M$ with degeneracy data `LevelLE M (M*p) ⊤ ⊤ 1` and `LevelLE M (M*p) ⊤ ⊤ p`, if $p\nmid M$, $\ell_0$ is prime and $\ell_0\nmid Mp$, then for all $g,h\in H^1(M,\top;A)$ with $i_1(g)+i_p(h)=0$ in $H^1(Mp,\top;A)$ both $g$ and $h$ are Eisenstein at $\ell_0$, i.e. $T_{\ell_0}$ acts on each as multiplication by $\ell_0+1$.
--
--   **The auxiliary prime $r$.** $r$ is prime, $r\ge 5$, $r\notin S$, $r\nmid Np$, $p\nmid r-1$, and for every valuation subring $P$ over $r$ and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $r$ for $P$, $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\sigma)^2\neq (r+1)^2$ (`hrρ`). Weight-two cusp forms of levels $N$ and $Np$ are assumed to have an integral structure, i.e. the $\mathbb C$-span of the lattice of forms with integral $q$-coefficients is everything.
--
--   **Eigensystems and $\mathcal O$-points.** $\theta_0$, $\theta_1$ are ring homomorphisms to $k$ from the anemic Hecke algebras [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) and [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra (N*p) 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebras of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}S_2(\Gamma_0(\cdot))$ generated by $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell$ outside $S$ not dividing the level and by $U_q$ for primes $q\notin S$ dividing it). The hypotheses `hθ₀`, `hθ₁` say that for every prime $\ell\notin S$ not dividing the respective level, every valuation subring $P$ over $\ell$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$, $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\theta_i(T_\ell)X+\ell$. The local rings [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) and [`CuspForm.heckeLocal (N*p) S 𝒪 θ₁`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) are the localisations of the corresponding $\mathcal O$-algebras at the multiplicative sets coming from the complements of the primes cut out by $\theta_0$, $\theta_1$; $\pi_{T_0}$, $\pi_{T_1}$ are $\mathcal O$-algebra maps from them to $\mathcal O$, and `hπ` requires $\pi_{T_1}(T_\ell)=\pi_{T_0}(T_\ell)$ for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid Np$.
--
--   **The ordinary package for $\rho'$.** $\rho'$ is an $\mathcal O$-adic representation of rank $2$ whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials away from $N$ and $S$ are $X^2-\pi_{T_0}(T_\ell)X+\ell$ (`hρ'`). Furthermore $P$ is a valuation subring lying over $p$, $L\subseteq\rho'.V$ is spanned by the first vector of some $\mathcal O$-basis (`hLb`), is stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$ (`hLD`), inertia acts trivially modulo $L$ (`hLI`), and $\alpha\in\mathcal O$ is a unit root in the sense that every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $p$ in the decomposition subgroup satisfies $\rho'(\sigma)v-\alpha v\in L$ for all $v$ (`hα`).
--
--   **The level-$N$ module.** $M_0$ is a module over $\mathcal O$ and over [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131), compatibly, finite and free over $\mathcal O$, with an $\mathcal O$-bilinear form $B_0$.
--
--   **The pairing family (`Bfam`, `hBfam`, `hBfam'`).** `Bfam` assigns to each level $M$, subgroup $H\le(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$ and datum `h₁ : LevelLE M M ⊤ H 1` an $\mathcal O$-bilinear form on the image in $H^1(M,H;\mathcal O)$, under the degree-one degeneracy map `iDegL`, of the parabolic homomorphisms at level $\Gamma_H(M,\top)$ (those vanishing on elements of trace square $4$). `hBfam` asserts, whenever $[(\mathbb Z/M)^\times:H]$ is a unit in $\mathcal O$: bijectivity of `Bfam M H h₁` as a map into the $\mathcal O$-dual; self-adjointness of the Hecke operators $T_\ell$ for $\ell$ prime or $\ell\mid M$, in the form $B(Tx,y)=B(x,Ty)$ for elements $Tx,Ty$ of the submodule representing $T_\ell x$, $T_\ell y$; and invariance of the submodule under the diamond operators `diamondL M H 𝒪 d`. `hBfam'` asserts the degeneracy adjointness $B_M(jy,x)=B_{M'}(y,ix)$ for $M\mid M'$, subgroups $H$, $H'$ with $H'$ the preimage of $H$, degrees $d,d'$ with $dd'=M'/M$, both indices units in $\mathcal O$, and $ix$, $jy$ representing `iDegL` of $x$ and `jDegL` of $y$.
--
--   **The level-$Nr$ corner data.** $H_0\le(\mathbb Z/Nr)^\times$ is the subgroup of units reducing to $1$ in $\mathbb Z/r$ (`hH₀`), with `h₁₀ : LevelLE (N*r) (N*r) ⊤ H₀ 1`. $\mathbb T_0$ is a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra acting compatibly on $H^1(Nr,H_0;\mathcal O)$, and `cd₀` is an `H1CornerData`: an idempotent splitting of $\mathbb T_0$, a chosen index `cd₀.idx`, and a level pairing on the corner ring and the corner submodule $e\cdot H^1(Nr,H_0;\mathcal O)$; $e_0$ identifies the corner ring with [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) as $\mathcal O$-algebras, and the corner module is finite and free over $\mathcal O$. The hypotheses on it are: `hT₀`, that for primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$ and $\ell\nmid Nr$ the element $e_0^{-1}(T_\ell)$ acts on the corner module as the operator `heckeT (N*r) H₀ ℓ`; `htp`, that $t_p$ is a unit of the corner ring acting both as `heckeT (N*r) H₀ p` and as `heckeTlower (N*r) H₀ p`; `hocc₀`, that the submodule of the corner module annihilated by $\ker(\pi_{T_0}\circ e_0)$ is non-zero; `hrk₀`, the rank identity $\mathrm{rk}_{\mathcal O}(\text{corner module})=\mathrm{rk}_{\mathcal O}(\text{that annihilated submodule})\cdot\mathrm{rk}_{\mathcal O}(\text{corner ring})$; `hgen`, that every $t\in\mathbb T_0$ acts on $H^1(Nr,H_0;\mathcal O)$ through an element of the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra generated by the range of [`CohCarrier.opFamily (N*r) H₀ S 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) (the operators $T_\ell$, $U_q$ and diamonds indexed by `Gen (N*r) S`); `hfaith`, that the corner ring acts faithfully on the corner module; and `hdia`, that the operators `diamondRaw (N*r) H₀ 𝒪 σ` for $\sigma\in\Gamma_0(Nr)$ fix the corner submodule pointwise.
--
--   **Generators, residual scalars and the corner criterion.** `tfull` lifts each generator $g$ of `Gen (N*r) S` to $\mathbb T_0$ and, for all $g$ subject to the side condition that $q\mid N$ in case $g=U_q$ (and no condition otherwise), `htfull` says $\mathrm{tfull}(g)$ acts as `opFamily` of $g$; `cfull` assigns to each such $g$ a scalar in $\mathcal O$ with $\mathrm{tfull}(g)-\mathrm{cfull}(g)$ in the ideal `cd₀.split.𝔪 cd₀.idx` (`hcfull`); `hcofull` says that a class $v\in H^1(Nr,H_0;\mathcal O)$ lies in the corner submodule as soon as for each such $g$ and each $k$ some power $(\mathrm{tfull}(g)-\mathrm{cfull}(g))^n$ carries $v$ into $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}^k\cdot H^1$; and `hcSigma` pins the residual scalars at the primes of $\Sigma$-type: for every prime $q$ dividing $Nr$ with $q\mid N$, $q\neq p$ and $q^2\mid N$, one has $\mathrm{cfull}(U_q)\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$.
--
--   **Non-Eisenstein saturation, parabolicity and transport.** `hne` asserts the existence of a prime $\ell_0$ with $\ell_0\nmid Nrp$ such that for every irreducible $\varpi\in\mathcal O$ and every $v$ in the corner module, $T_{\ell_0}v-(\ell_0+1)v\in\varpi\cdot H^1(Nr,H_0;\mathcal O)$ forces $v\in\varpi\cdot(\text{corner module})$. `hW₀` says the corner submodule is contained in the image of the parabolic homomorphisms under `iDegL (N*r) (N*r) ⊤ H₀ 1`, and `hP₀` says that `cd₀.pairing.B` is the restriction of `Bfam (N*r) H₀ h₁₀` along this inclusion. Finally $s_0$ is an $\mathcal O$-linear isomorphism from the corner module to $M_0$, equivariant for the corner-ring action transported through $e_0$ (`hs₀`), and carrying `cd₀.pairing.B` to $B_0$ (`hB₀`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist a type $M_1$ with an abelian group structure, a module structure over [`CuspForm.heckeLocal (N*p) S 𝒪 θ₁`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131), an $\mathcal O$-module structure forming a scalar tower with it, finiteness and freeness over $\mathcal O$, and an $\mathcal O$-bilinear form $B_1$ on $M_1$, such that:
--
--   (1) $B_1$ is self-adjoint for the whole Hecke ring: $B_1(tm,m')=B_1(m,tm')$ for all $t$ in [`CuspForm.heckeLocal (N*p) S 𝒪 θ₁`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) and all $m,m'\in M_1$;
--
--   (2) $B_1$ is bijective, i.e. perfect as a map of $M_1$ into its $\mathcal O$-dual;
--
--   (3) the submodule of $M_1$ annihilated by $\ker\pi_{T_1}$ is non-zero;
--
--   (4) $\mathrm{rk}_{\mathcal O}M_1=\mathrm{rk}_{\mathcal O}\bigl(M_1[\ker\pi_{T_1}]\bigr)$ times the $\mathcal O$-rank of [`CuspForm.heckeLocal (N*p) S 𝒪 θ₁`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131);
--
--   (5) and there are $\mathcal O$-linear maps $i:M_0\to M_1$, $j:M_1\to M_0$ and an element $\Delta$ of [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) with: $B_0(j m',m)=B_1(m',i\,m)$ for all $m'\in M_1$, $m\in M_0$; $j(i\,m)=\Delta\cdot m$ for all $m\in M_0$; the image under $i$ of the submodule of $M_0$ annihilated by $\ker\pi_{T_0}$ (restricted to $\mathcal O$-scalars) equal to the submodule of $M_1$ annihilated by $\ker\pi_{T_1}$; and the equality of principal ideals $(\pi_{T_0}\Delta)=(\alpha^2-1)$ in $\mathcal O$.
--
--   This is the $p$-level-raising rung of the Ihara tower: starting from a Hecke module $M_0$ of level $N$ with a perfect self-adjoint pairing realised inside the parabolic cohomology of level $Nr$, it produces the corresponding module at level $Np$ for the $U_p$-eigensystem $\theta_1$, together with the degeneracy pair $(i,j)$, the composite $j\circ i=\Delta$ and the identification of $\pi_{T_0}(\Delta)$ with the unit-root factor $\alpha^2-1$. It feeds the assembly of the ordinary presentation in [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.bijective_and_exists_presentation_of_ordinaryCondition_of_finiteAt_of_not_cube_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.bijective_and_exists_presentation_of_ordinaryCondition_of_finiteAt_of_not_cube_dvd), where this factor becomes the $\eta$-invariant comparison between the $p$-old and level-$N$ congruence modules.
